      "message": "fix(app): a touch probe is not judged against the machine's spindle range\n\nThe machine check compared every tool's catalog rpm with the mounted\nmachine's spindle window, so a probe's token rpm (1) refused every\nprobing program on a machine stating a minimum - the Tormach 770MX's\n175 rpm among them - though the post never commands it. The check now\nreads the speed the program commands, posting::posted_rpm (0 for a\nprobe, the tool's own rpm for a cutter), the same answer the post uses.\n\nPinned by probe_spindle_range::{a_probe_program_passes_the_spindle_range_of_a_tormach,\na_probe_posts_no_speed_and_a_cutter_its_own,\na_cutter_below_the_minimum_is_still_refused_beside_a_probe}.\n\nFixes #565\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
